Keep a shared number as empty text.
Place "1432219" into number.
Keep a shared removes as 0.
Set removes to 3.
Keep a shared chosen as 0.
To choose.
Set chosen to -1.
The last is the last position of number.
The limit is last minus 1.
For every spot from 0 to limit.
The leftdigit is the digit value of character spot of number.
The rightdigit is the digit value of character (spot plus 1) of number.
If chosen is -1 and leftdigit is more than rightdigit, set chosen to spot.

To carve.
Choose.
The last is the last position of number.
If chosen is -1, set chosen to last.
The head is the slice of number from 0 to chosen.
The tail is the slice of number from chosen plus 1 to last plus 1.
The joined is empty text.
Place head into joined.
Place tail into joined.
Set number to joined.

For every step from 1 to removes.
Carve.

The size is the number of characters in number.
The zero is character 0 of "0".
Repeat while size is more than 1.
The first is character 0 of number.
If first is not zero, break.
The last is the last position of number.
The joined is the slice of number from 1 to last plus 1.
Set number to joined.
Set size to the number of characters in number.

Show number.
